[
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "# [07] Version Control Git",
      "block_property": "paragraph"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "📋 Panoramica",
      "block_property": "heading_2"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "Materia dedicata al controllo di versione distribuito con Git. Copre l'intero flusso di lavoro: repository locale, branching, repository remoti (GitHub/GitLab) e client grafici. Approccio progressivo dai fondamenti agli strumenti GUI.",
      "block_property": "paragraph"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "**Tecnologie**: Git (CLI), GitHub, GitLab, Git GUI (Sourcetree, GitKraken, VS Code)",
      "block_property": "paragraph"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "block_property": "divider"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "📚 Indice degli argomenti",
      "block_property": "heading_2"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "1. Fondamenti di Version Control",
      "block_property": "heading_3"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "**Cos'è il version control**: tracciamento delle modifiche ai file nel tempo",
      "block_property": "bulleted_list_item"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "**VCS Centralizzato** (SVN, CVS): server singolo, single point of failure",
      "block_property": "bulleted_list_item"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "**VCS Distribuito** (Git, Mercurial): ogni clone è un backup completo",
      "block_property": "bulleted_list_item"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "**Concetti base**:",
      "block_property": "bulleted_list_item"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "- Repository (repo): contenitore del progetto",
      "block_property": "paragraph"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "- Commit: snapshot dello stato dei file",
      "block_property": "paragraph"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "- Hash SHA-1: identificatore univoco di ogni commit",
      "block_property": "paragraph"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "**Flusso base**:",
      "block_property": "bulleted_list_item"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "  git init                    # crea nuovo repository",
      "block_property": "paragraph"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "  git add <file>              # staging area",
      "block_property": "paragraph"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "  git commit -m \"messaggio\"   # salva snapshot",
      "block_property": "paragraph"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "  git log                     # cronologia commit",
      "block_property": "paragraph"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "  git status                  # stato attuale",
      "block_property": "paragraph"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "2. Git Locale e Branch",
      "block_property": "heading_3"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "**Working directory → Staging area → Repository** (tre stati di Git)",
      "block_property": "bulleted_list_item"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "**Branch**: puntatore mobile a un commit; ramo di sviluppo indipendente",
      "block_property": "bulleted_list_item"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "**Comandi branch**:",
      "block_property": "bulleted_list_item"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "  git branch <nome>           # crea branch",
      "block_property": "paragraph"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "  git checkout <nome>         # switcha a branch",
      "block_property": "paragraph"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "  git switch <nome>           # alternativa moderna (Git 2.23+)",
      "block_property": "paragraph"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "  git merge <branch>          # unisce branch nel corrente",
      "block_property": "paragraph"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "**Merge**: automatico (fast-forward o 3-way) o manuale (conflitto da risolvere)",
      "block_property": "bulleted_list_item"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "**Conflitti**: succedono quando stesso file modificato in due branch",
      "block_property": "bulleted_list_item"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "  <<<<<<< HEAD",
      "block_property": "paragraph"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "  nostro codice",
      "block_property": "paragraph"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "  =======",
      "block_property": "paragraph"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "  loro codice",
      "block_property": "paragraph"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "  >>>>>>> feature-branch",
      "block_property": "paragraph"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "**Stash**: salva modifiche temporanee senza commit",
      "block_property": "bulleted_list_item"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "  git stash        # salva",
      "block_property": "paragraph"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "  git stash pop    # ripristina",
      "block_property": "paragraph"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "3. Git Remoto e Repository Online",
      "block_property": "heading_3"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "**git clone**: copia un repository remoto in locale",
      "block_property": "bulleted_list_item"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "**git remote**: gestisce connessioni a repository remoti",
      "block_property": "bulleted_list_item"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "**git push**: invia commit locali al remoto",
      "block_property": "bulleted_list_item"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "**git pull**: recupera e unisce (fetch + merge) dal remoto",
      "block_property": "bulleted_list_item"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "**git fetch**: recupera senza unire",
      "block_property": "bulleted_list_item"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "**Flusso collaborativo base**:",
      "block_property": "bulleted_list_item"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "  git clone <url>",
      "block_property": "paragraph"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "  git checkout -b feature/nuova-funzionalità",
      "block_property": "paragraph"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "  # ...lavoro...",
      "block_property": "paragraph"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "  git add . && git commit -m \"feat: aggiunta funzionalità X\"",
      "block_property": "paragraph"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "  git push origin feature/nuova-funzionalità",
      "block_property": "paragraph"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "  # → aprire Pull Request su GitHub",
      "block_property": "paragraph"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "**GitHub/Lab**: fork, pull request, code review, issues, actions/CI",
      "block_property": "bulleted_list_item"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "4. Git GUI e Client Grafici",
      "block_property": "heading_3"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "**GitHub Desktop**: semplice, integrazione GitHub nativa",
      "block_property": "bulleted_list_item"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "**Sourcetree**: visuale, branching grafico, flow Git-flow",
      "block_property": "bulleted_list_item"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "**GitKraken**: cross-platform, integrazione issue tracker",
      "block_property": "bulleted_list_item"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "**VS Code Git**: built-in, staging visuale, diff editor, branch switcher",
      "block_property": "bulleted_list_item"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "**gitg / GitEye / Git Cola**: alternative Linux/lightweight",
      "block_property": "bulleted_list_item"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "block_property": "divider"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "⚡ Punti Chiave",
      "block_property": "heading_2"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "**Commit atomici e frequenti**: un commit = un'unità logica di modifica",
      "block_property": "numbered_list_item"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "**Messaggi di commit chiari**: imperativo, prima riga <72 caratteri",
      "block_property": "numbered_list_item"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "**Mai pushare su main/master diretto**: usare feature branch + PR",
      "block_property": "numbered_list_item"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "**Pull sempre prima di push**: `git pull --rebase` per cronologia lineare",
      "block_property": "numbered_list_item"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "**`.gitignore`**: non committare mai file binari, secret, `node_modules/`, `.env`",
      "block_property": "numbered_list_item"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "**Non fare rebase su branch pubblici**: altera la cronologia",
      "block_property": "numbered_list_item"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "block_property": "divider"
    }
  },
  {
    "content_block": {
      "content": "📎 Risorse Collegate",
      "block_property": "heading_2"
    }
  },
